Implemented Features
Dashboard (Home)
Displays Total Balance, Total Income, Total Expenses, Monthly Budget, and Remaining Budget with an animated progress bar.
Shows active budget warning banners, quick actions (Add Expense, Add Income, Savings, and Reports), and Recent Transactions.
Income & Expense Management
Add, edit, and delete Expenses (Food, Transportation, Education, Bills, Shopping, Entertainment, Health, Other) and Income (Salary, Freelance, Business, Allowance, Investment, Gift, Other) with amount validation, description/note, and a Material 3 Date Picker.
Budget Management (Budget)
Configure Daily, Weekly, and Monthly budget limits, per-category monthly spending caps, and an alert threshold percentage.
Tracks spent vs. remaining amounts, triggers in-app budget warning banners and local Android notifications (with Android 13+ POST_NOTIFICATIONS runtime permission handling), and visualizes daily/weekly/monthly spending alongside savings progress.
Savings Goals (Savings)
Create, edit, and delete savings goals with target amounts, optional target dates, color themes, Add Contribution deposits, animated progress bars, and recent contribution history.
Transaction History (Transactions)
Search by description or category, filter by transaction type, category, or date (All Time, Today, This Week, This Month, or custom date picker), sort (Newest, Oldest, Highest Amount, Lowest Amount), and edit or delete records.
Financial Reports (Budget → Reports / Home → Reports)
Daily, Weekly, and Monthly expense totals, averages, and interactive bar charts.
Income vs. Expenses comparison chart with net cashflow and savings rate.
Category Breakdown donut chart and per-category percentages, plus a Savings Goals Report.
Settings (Settings)
Switch currency (USD, PHP, EUR, GBP, JPY, CAD, AUD), choose theme (System, Light, Dark), toggle budget warning notifications, optionally load sample budget data for exploration, or clear all local records.
Adaptive Design & Custom Branding
Material Design 3 emerald-and-gold theme, bundled typography, custom adaptive launcher icon, edge-to-edge insets, bottom navigation bar on phones, and a NavigationRail on wide screens.
